anya_onboard: Ran into two annoying things in the node quickstart today: 1) first few startup logs show RequestId=null, 2) redaction missed a long-looking API key embedded inside JSON -> customer-facing sample app leaked one in my run.

lee_sdk: ouch. can you paste the minimal repro + logger config?

anya_onboard: minimal repro attached inline. It's the sample-app with rws.init at top:
```
// index.js
const rws = require('redwood-sdk');
require('dotenv').config();

rws.init({
  otel: true,
  logging: { level: 'info', redaction: [/sk_[a-zA-Z0-9]{10,}/] }
});

const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(rws.middleware.logger);

app.post('/v1/events', (req, res) => {
  console.log('raw body', req.body); // sometimes prints before reqid attached
  req.log.info('handling event', {body: req.body});
  res.status(200).send({ok:true});
});
```
Output: first console line shows entire key `sk_test_verylongKEY123456` and request id null. the second structured log has reqid and key redacted.

ops_emma: could be race between our console shim and async otel startup. we only swap global console after otel instrumentation finishes, and express logs may run earlier. also our redaction currently hooks into logger calls, not raw stdout.

lee_sdk: yep. two issues: (A) console/console.log gets called before our wrapper installed; (B) our redaction regex uses a JS RegExp but we only apply it to strings passed through rws logger; if frameworks use console directly or JSON.stringify later, we miss it.

anya_onboard: i also observed that during cold start some library debug logs happen before our init finishes and those prints expose keys copied into env vars -> quickstart is leaking when people paste examples. bad first impression.

lee_sdk: quick mitigation: 1) make console shim synchronous and first thing in rws.init (before starting async otel setup), 2) add an stdout transform fallback that applies redaction regexes to any string written to process.stdout/stderr. that way even console.log gets scrubbed.

ops_emma: agree. add a small opt-in flag `init({forceSyncConsoleShim:true})` for now so we can ship without delaying otel init; default false for now but we can flip once tested. also add a e2e that starts sample app and greps stdout for token patterns.

lee_sdk: long-term: unify redaction rules so they apply at both logger layer and low-level write() hook. also add deterministic requestId assignment earlier in middleware chain: install a tiny sync stub that sets req.id before any user middleware. express ordering is fragile; we should document "install rws.middleware.logger as first app.use" in onboarding.

diag-bot: created issue RW-5577: "synchronous console shim + stdout-level redaction + early reqid stub + quickstart doc update" assigned to lee_sdk, severity=medium.

anya_onboard: i patched my local rws.init to call a small consoleShim.install() synchronously before otel promises. retested: first log now shows reqid=abc123 and key replaced with `[REDACTED]`.

ops_emma: please add the local repro and output to RW-5577 so we can add unit tests. also file a follow-up to audit python and go SDKs for same stdout race (parity RW-5578).

lee_sdk: will do. i'll also add a one-paragraph note in quickstart: "avoid raw console.log in production; use rws.logger and ensure SDK init order is before app.listen" along with code snippet showing the recommended ordering.

anya_onboard: thanks all. marking sample-app onboarding friction as addressed locally; will watch for other leaks in CI e2e once RW-5577 lands. :+1:
